2026-10-28T17:47:57.2484434Z {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgV4AAwLbhHLDtXBW1bLe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NWsTrkTp2qHW35ys2T1726","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6008,"cache_read_input_tokens":24852,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6008,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33df9f6a-5e06-4271-a161-601a4ef8de19","uuid":"b125d4ba-c015-431c-b2a3-005709d19719","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:47:57.245Z","request_id":"req_011CgV4AAaGYpnhGtVPDyxuX"}
2026-10-28T17:47:57.2700838Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NWsTrkTp2qHW35ys2T1726","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"number\": 34,\n3\t  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/34\",\n4\t  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n5\t  \"title\": \"aws_lambda_function: image_uri is not reset to the previous value when UpdateFunctionCode fails (unlike s3_bucket/s3_key/s3_object_version, fixed in `#42695`/`#42829`)\",\n6\t  \"body\": \"### Terraform and AWS Provider Version\\n\\n```\\nhashicorp/aws v5.100.0 (confirmed still present at v5.100.0's tagged source; the fix in #42829 that resolved the analogous S3-based issue does not touch this code path)\\n```\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n`aws_lambda_function`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `UpdateFunctionCode` fails for a container-image-based Lambda function, `image_uri` in state should be reset back to its previous (last-known-good) value \\u2014 matching the fix already applied to `s3_bucket`/`s3_key`/`s3_object_version` in `#42695`/`#42829`.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\n`image_uri` is left holding the new (unapplied) value in state after a failed `UpdateFunctionCode` call, even though the real Lambda function was never updated. A subsequent `terraform plan` reports no changes needed, hiding real drift.\\n\\n### Root cause (confirmed by reading `internal/service/lambda/function.go` at the v5.100.0 tag)\\n\\nIn `resourceFunctionUpdate`, the code-update branch handles three code-source types \\u2014 `filename` (ZIP), `image_uri` (container image), and `s3_bucket`/`s3_key`/`s3_object_version` (S3 object). After `conn.UpdateFunctionCode(ctx, input)` fails, the error-handling block resets state only for the S3-based attributes, and only for one specific error class:\\n\\n```go\\nif err != nil {\\n    if errs.IsAErrorMessageContains[*awstypes.InvalidParameterValueException](err, \\\"Error occurred while GetObject.\\\") {\\n        // As s3_bucket, s3_key and s3_object_version aren't set in resourceFunctionRead(), don't ovewrite the last known good values.\\n        for _, key := range []string{names.AttrS3Bucket, \\\"s3_key\\\", \\\"s3_object_version\\\"} {\\n            old, _ := d.GetChange(key)\\n            d.Set(key, old)\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    return sdkdiag.AppendErrorf(diags, \\\"updating Lambda Function (%s) code: %s\\\", d.Id(), err)\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThere is no equivalent branch for `image_uri`. Like `s3_bucket`/`s3_key`/`s3_object_version`, `image_uri` is not set in `resourceFunctionRead()` (it's not re-derived from a refresh), so on any `UpdateFunctionCode` failure \\u2014 not just the specific S3 `GetObject` error class this block currently checks \\u2014 `image_uri` is left at its new, never-actually-applied value.\\n\\n### Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. Create a container-image-based `aws_lambda_function`.\\n2. Remove `lambda:UpdateFunctionCode` from the applying principal's IAM policy.\\n3. Change `image_uri` in config to point at a different tag/digest.\\n4. `terraform apply` \\u2014 fails with `AccessDeniedException` on `UpdateFunctionCode`, as expected.\\n5. `terraform plan` \\u2014 reports \\\"No changes\\\", even though the real function's code was never updated.\\n\\n### Suggested fix\\n\\nExtend the reset block (or apply it unconditionally on any `UpdateFunctionCode` error, matching the reasoning already discussed on `#42695` by `@tabito-hara` and `@vtstanescu` \\u2014 the error-class check may not be necessary at all, since none of these attributes are ever refreshed from the API) to also reset `image_uri`:\\n\\n```go\\nif err != nil {\\n    for _, key := range []string{names.AttrS3Bucket, \\\"s3_key\\\", \\\"s3_object_version\\\", \\\"image_uri\\\"} {\\n        old, _ := d.GetChange(key)\\n        d.Set(key, old)\\n    }\\n    return sdkdiag.AppendErrorf(diags, \\\"updating Lambda Function (%s) code: %s\\\", d.Id(), err)\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Would you like to implement a fix?\\n\\nYes, if a maintainer confirms this is welcome as a follow-up to `#42829`'s pattern.\\n\",\n7\t  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n8\t  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n9\t  \"labels\": [],\n10\t  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:09:52Z\",\n11\t  \"as_of\": \"2026-08-06T02:10:29Z\"\n12\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33df9f6a-5e06-4271-a161-601a4ef8de19","uuid":"6f829f91-1664-4e2c-adcc-53785a6f4a7e","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:47:57.263Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json","content":"{\n  \"number\": 34,\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/34\",\n  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n  \"title\": \"aws_lambda_function: image_uri is not reset to the previous value when UpdateFunctionCode fails (unlike s3_bucket/s3_key/s3_object_version, fixed in `#42695`/`#42829`)\",\n  \"body\": \"### Terraform and AWS Provider Version\\n\\n```\\nhashicorp/aws v5.100.0 (confirmed still present at v5.100.0's tagged source; the fix in #42829 that resolved the analogous S3-based issue does not touch this code path)\\n```\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n`aws_lambda_function`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `UpdateFunctionCode` fails for a container-image-based Lambda function, `image_uri` in state should be reset back to its previous (last-known-good) value \\u2014 matching the fix already applied to `s3_bucket`/`s3_key`/`s3_object_version` in `#42695`/`#42829`.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\n`image_uri` is left holding the new (unapplied) value in state after a failed `UpdateFunctionCode` call, even though the real Lambda function was never updated. A subsequent `terraform plan` reports no changes needed, hiding real drift.\\n\\n### Root cause (confirmed by reading `internal/service/lambda/function.go` at the v5.100.0 tag)\\n\\nIn `resourceFunctionUpdate`, the code-update branch handles three code-source types \\u2014 `filename` (ZIP), `image_uri` (container image), and `s3_bucket`/`s3_key`/`s3_object_version` (S3 object). After `conn.UpdateFunctionCode(ctx, input)` fails, the error-handling block resets state only for the S3-based attributes, and only for one specific error class:\\n\\n```go\\nif err != nil {\\n    if errs.IsAErrorMessageContains[*awstypes.InvalidParameterValueException](err, \\\"Error occurred while GetObject.\\\") {\\n        // As s3_bucket, s3_key and s3_object_version aren't set in resourceFunctionRead(), don't ovewrite the last known good values.\\n        for _, key := range []string{names.AttrS3Bucket, \\\"s3_key\\\", \\\"s3_object_version\\\"} {\\n            old, _ := d.GetChange(key)\\n            d.Set(key, old)\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    return sdkdiag.AppendErrorf(diags, \\\"updating Lambda Function (%s) code: %s\\\", d.Id(), err)\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThere is no equivalent branch for `image_uri`. Like `s3_bucket`/`s3_key`/`s3_object_version`, `image_uri` is not set in `resourceFunctionRead()` (it's not re-derived from a refresh), so on any `UpdateFunctionCode` failure \\u2014 not just the specific S3 `GetObject` error class this block currently checks \\u2014 `image_uri` is left at its new, never-actually-applied value.\\n\\n### Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. Create a container-image-based `aws_lambda_function`.\\n2. Remove `lambda:UpdateFunctionCode` from the applying principal's IAM policy.\\n3. Change `image_uri` in config to point at a different tag/digest.\\n4. `terraform apply` \\u2014 fails with `AccessDeniedException` on `UpdateFunctionCode`, as expected.\\n5. `terraform plan` \\u2014 reports \\\"No changes\\\", even though the real function's code was never updated.\\n\\n### Suggested fix\\n\\nExtend the reset block (or apply it unconditionally on any `UpdateFunctionCode` error, matching the reasoning already discussed on `#42695` by `@tabito-hara` and `@vtstanescu` \\u2014 the error-class check may not be necessary at all, since none of these attributes are ever refreshed from the API) to also reset `image_uri`:\\n\\n```go\\nif err != nil {\\n    for _, key := range []string{names.AttrS3Bucket, \\\"s3_key\\\", \\\"s3_object_version\\\", \\\"image_uri\\\"} {\\n        old, _ := d.GetChange(key)\\n        d.Set(key, old)\\n    }\\n    return sdkdiag.AppendErrorf(diags, \\\"updating Lambda Function (%s) code: %s\\\", d.Id(), err)\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Would you like to implement a fix?\\n\\nYes, if a maintainer confirms this is welcome as a follow-up to `#42829`'s pattern.\\n\",\n  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"labels\": [],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:09:52Z\",\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-08-06T02:10:29Z\"\n}","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NWsTrkTp2qHW35ys2T1726","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
